      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "Affects `RequestQueueSingleton$TLSSocketFactory.<init>` in `app/src/main/java/xyz/zedler/patrick/grocy/web/RequestQueueSingleton.java`.\n\nI found that the TLS socket factory obtains an `SSLContext` and initializes it twice: once with null values, then again with the client-certificate key manager, memorizing trust manager, and secure random source. That breaks the `SSLContextSpec` tool rule’s expected call order.\n\nI removed the preliminary null initialization so the context is initialized once with the existing TLS configuration before its socket factory is created. This is safe because the existing key manager, trust manager, secure random source, and `\"TLS\"` context selection remain unchanged.\n\nI found this while running the app under RVSec, a runtime checker for how apps use the Java crypto and TLS APIs.\n\nThe project builds with this change (`assembleDebug`).\n\nI'm a Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), working on a research project on Android app analysis. Happy to adjust this to the project's conventions.",
